      "sequence_position": 15,
      "problem": "$$\n\nCalculate $\\int \\frac{\\pi }{e-e{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x$ for $|x|>1.$",
      "worked_solution": "$$\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic cotangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\pi }{e-e{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{\\pi }{e(1-{x}^{2})}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{e}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{e}\\operatorname{arcoth}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
